## Why Vows Are the Hardest Sound in the Whole Day

A ceremony asks more of a sound system than a reception does. Guests are seated, listening for a single voice at conversational volume, not dance music at a volume that forgives a rough edge. Outdoors, open air has no walls to reflect sound back toward the seats, so a voice that would fill a small room thins out over open grass or sand. At a beach ceremony, wind and the waves behind the couple compete with the officiant for the same air, and a PA that is not placed and leveled correctly loses the vows to that background noise, not to a lack of volume.

The fix our technician uses is placement, not tenting: speakers positioned close to the seated guests rather than one system pushed from a distance, with levels set for the specific spot, wind direction and crowd size on the day. This page keeps to that ceremony specific angle. For the fuller outdoor picture, power, curfews and how a coastal terrace changes equipment placement across the whole day, see our [outdoor wedding rental considerations](/blog/outdoor-wedding-rental-considerations/) guide.

## Processional and Recessional Music Through the PA

The walk down the aisle and the walk back out both run on a music cue, and MEG's job is amplifying that cue, not choosing or performing it. A live musician, a guitarist or a string player, gets amplified through the same PA the officiant's microphone uses. MEG does not provide the musician. A fully recorded playlist runs through the same system instead, timed to the processional and recessional moments the couple sets. Either way, our part is the hardware and the timing through it, not the performance.

## Ambient Lighting as Atmosphere, Not Decor

The Wedding Pack's fairy lights and warm LED strings add atmosphere to a ceremony space, not structure to it. We are not a decor provider: no arch, no backdrop, no draping, no furniture. The lighting layers a warm glow onto whatever the venue or a decorator has already set up, a genuinely different service from supplying the setting itself, and one worth being clear about before you book us expecting the latter. See our [lighting ideas for wedding rentals](/blog/lighting-ideas-for-wedding-rentals/) guide for how those fairy lights compare to the Eco Pack's RGBW spotlights.

